Full fix — five things:
1. your routing catch: `<a href>` → Next's `<Link href>`, restoring client-side navigation instead of full reloads;
2. no layout at all → horizontal row with wrapping (`flex-wrap`) so it degrades gracefully on narrow screens instead of overflowing;
3. no visual separation from page content above → `border-t` + vertical padding;
4. muted-to-full-color hover, standard treatment for this kind of secondary nav;
5. wrapped in `<nav aria-label="...">` — a footer with multiple links is navigation, and the label distinguishes it from the page's primary nav for screen reader users.
Rewriting:
